HyperPod — heterogeneous 3-node → 2-node same-request recovery (30 Oct 2026)
============================================================================
Nodes:
  Controller/local: ROG Linux, RTX 3050 CUDA
  Remote 1: Windows TUF (worker-KAMALESH), RTX 4050 CUDA, 192.168.1.5
  Remote 2: M4 Mac (worker-Krishs-MacBook-Air), Metal RPC, 192.168.1.13
Network: trusted local Wi-Fi.
Model: Llama 3.2 3B Q4_K_M.

Initial three-machine placement from llama.cpp:
  CPU_Mapped                              308 MiB
  CUDA0 (ROG)                             552 MiB
  RPC0[192.168.1.13:50052] (M4 Mac)       968 MiB
  RPC0[192.168.1.5:50052] (TUF)           398 MiB
  29/29 layers; split=true; ready after 82 s.

Scheduler strategy: llama.cpp-auto (remote free VRAM unavailable).
Reason: macOS telemetry measured 16,384 MiB total unified memory, battery and AC,
but did not expose a trustworthy Metal free-memory value. HyperPod supplied no
invented custom weight. llama.cpp probed the remote devices itself.

Test request:
  "Write a detailed 250-word explanation of why collaboration matters in
   engineering teams." (n_predict=420)

Physical failure:
  Operator pressed Ctrl+C in the Mac ggml-rpc-server while the request was
  in flight. The Mac Rust worker remained alive, intentionally proving that an
  agent heartbeat alone does not prove its RPC accelerator is available.

Recovery log:
  23:15:02 llama-server gen 1 exited: signal: aborted (core dumped)
  23:15:02 infer attempt 1 recognized node death and re-ran the same request
  23:15:02 pool skipped Mac RPC (worker heartbeat OK, RPC unreachable)
  23:15:02 launched gen 2 over TUF only, plus local ROG
             measured scheduler weights=4763,3204; reserve=512 MiB/device
  23:15:35 gen 2 ready after 33 seconds

Recovered two-machine placement:
  CPU_Mapped                             308 MiB
  CUDA0 (ROG RTX 3050)                  896 MiB
  RPC0[192.168.1.5:50052] (TUF)       1022 MiB
  split=true

The ORIGINAL HTTP request returned successfully:
  ok=true; text length=1,937 characters; elapsed=75.68 seconds.
  Answer begins: "Collaboration is a vital component of engineering teams, as
  it fosters a culture of open communication, diverse perspectives, and
  collective problem-solving..."

Conclusion:
  Verified heterogeneous ROG + Windows CUDA + macOS Metal placement; physical
  Mac RPC loss; true 3-node → 2-node distributed rebuild; and automatic retry
  of the same in-flight request. This is restart-and-retry recovery, not
  token/KV-cache continuation.
